+                   * compare says "nothing in front of me": lit. Measured on our stack the surface we
+                   * read back is NOT cleared to 1: min=0 max=1 with nz between 0.080 and 0.098, i.e.
+                   * 90 percent of the texels are zero. With a zero background the comparison can never
+                   * produce occlusion, and a fetch that yields the raw zero is exactly the "shadows
+                   * much lighter than on real hardware" symptom. Mode 3 maps the empty texels to the
+                   * far value before uploading, which is what a cleared surface would have given us.
+                   * A legitimate depth of exactly 0 (geometry on the near plane) is remapped too:
+                   * acceptable for the experiment, documented here. */
+              }
+              make_client_context_current();
+
+              if (read_ok)
+              {
+                  /* nvlegacy: which mipmap level we write. Measured: the source is a correct shadow
+                   * map (min=0.75 max=1, mean=0.997519, 4152688 of 4194304 texels at the far value)
+                   * while the object the Mesa inspector later samples ends up min=0 max=1 mean=0.040
+                   * nz=0.080, i.e. the far background is gone. The prime suspect is the level: this
+                   * code passed pbuffer->mipmap_level, and if that is not zero we write into another
+                   * level and leave level 0 as the application allocated it. */
+                  int nv_level = pbuffer->mipmap_level > 0 ? pbuffer->mipmap_level : 0;
+
+                  funcs->p_glBindTexture( target, prev_tex );
+                  funcs->p_glPixelStorei( GL_UNPACK_ALIGNMENT, 1 );
+                  /* nvlegacy: WINE_NV_PBUFFER_RT_DEPTH_RESPEC, see the note above the helper. */
+                  {
+                      GLenum internal_fmt = nvlegacy_pbuffer_rt_depth_respec();
+                      if (internal_fmt && nv_respec_done( pbuffer, (GLuint)prev_tex ) == FALSE)
+                      {
+                          funcs->p_glTexImage2D( target, nv_level, internal_fmt, width, height, 0,
